  "findings": {
    "flux2AndKrea": "Footprint after unload grows over the first three cycles (FLUX.2 368, 531, 683 MiB; Krea 398, 477, 572 MiB) and is then flat, while live malloc stays within 12 MiB of the baseline. The rest is freed large allocations that the macOS allocator keeps dirty (\"Malloc Large (empty)\"); malloc_zone_pressure_relief does not return them. With the allocator's large cache disabled (MallocLargeCache=0, a diagnostic) the residue is 27 MiB (FLUX.2) and 36 MiB (Krea) above the baseline from cycle 1. Not a Kit or Core AI leak.",
    "kokoro2048": "Footprint is still 8.3-8.6 GB at the moment unload() returns and falls to 0.09-0.28 GB within 2 s. Metal currentAllocatedSize stays at 8,312 MiB from cycle 2 (10,312 after cycle 1) without growing, while the footprint tool shows about 2 MiB of IOAccelerator memory and system wired memory is flat: the counter does not mean the memory is held. Kit allocates no Metal memory in this path.",
    "kokoroStandard": "One-time 70 MiB after cycle 1, then within 3 MiB over five cycles; Metal 13 MiB."
  }
}
